Build the DS core against a current toolchain.

Two independent breakages, both from devkitA64 having moved to GCC 15.2.0
while the buildbot stays on something older.

    rsemaphore.c:104:7: error: 'return' with no value, in function returning
    non-void [-Wreturn-mismatch]

ssem_trywait returns bool and its null check returns nothing. GCC made this
an error by default in 14. false is the only defensible value: a semaphore
that does not exist has not been acquired, and every caller reads the result
as "did I get it".

    libretro.cpp:60:10: error: 'time' was not declared in this scope

srand(time(NULL)) with no <ctime>. It used to arrive transitively through
one of the other headers and no longer does, which is a normal consequence
of libstdc++ tightening what it pulls in rather than anything melonDS did.

Neither is a Switch-specific problem; both would bite any platform building
this with a recent compiler.

diff --git a/src/libretro/libretro-common/rthreads/rsemaphore.c b/src/libretro/libretro-common/rthreads/rsemaphore.c
